    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d512">

                <pb facs="0616" n="358" sameAs="frus:frus1915Supp/pg358"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. F.W.462.11T41</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Germany</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Gerard</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1915-04-06T16:00:00-05:00">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 6, 1915, 4 p. m.</hi>
                        </date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1471. American citizen reported drowned when British steamship <hi
                        rendition="#italic">Falaba</hi> was sunk March 28 by German submarine. Has
                    there been <pb facs="0617" n="359" xml:id="pg359"/> official report of incident?
                    If not, can you obtain by discreet and unofficial inquiries German account, and
                    particularly reason for torpedoing <hi rendition="#italic">Falaba</hi> before
                    crew and passengers had time to withdraw in boats to a distance from vessel
                    sufficient to insure safety when <hi rendition="#italic">Falaba</hi> sank? You
                    are urgently requested to report as soon as possible.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Bryan</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
